  "_comment": "The single source of truth for MonitorCLT signals. Consolidates the scattered configs (score weights, signals_catalog, env_sources) into one prioritizable list. Each signal carries: family, dimension (the five-score bucket), source, availability, cadence, and the four scoring attributes value/reliability/effort/legality. prioritize.py ranks 'what to build next' from these. This is a seed (~70 signals); the full taxonomy targets 150-250 -- but the point is prioritization, not completeness. availability: wired|derived|free-add|env-free|sos-paid|rod-browser|court-browser|mls-paid|not-obtainable. status: built|config-ready|not-started. value/reliability/effort are 1-5. legality: ok|sensitive.",

